From 3a4c9e5be7f17b5c24c532faf1bad37d9bed55b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: norm wasm <blake@comatri.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 23:52:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] native: build the core for wasm32-wasi

zig build -Dtarget=wasm32-wasi produces lib/wasm32-wasi/opentui.wasm, a
WASI reactor module exporting every FFI symbol plus its function table.

- miniaudio is compiled out on wasm (audio-stub.zig reports no device)
- single-threaded: BufferedBackend never spawns its render thread
- yoga builds with -fno-exceptions -fno-rtti
- fixed-size linear memory (initial == max, -Dwasm-memory-mb, default
  256): JS keeps long-lived typed-array views over native buffers and
  memory.grow would detach them; page_allocator is routed through libc
  malloc, which carves the preallocated heap
- opentuiWasmAlloc/opentuiWasmFree for staging JS buffers
- StyledChunk.text_len/link_len and ExternalCapabilities.term_*_len are
  u64 to match the JS struct definitions on 32-bit targets (unchanged on
  64-bit hosts)
- text buffers copy borrowed (owned=false) memory on wasm, since JS
  buffers only reach linear memory as short-lived staged copies
- loadFile's u64 file size is cast to usize
